{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b06b4bb56cb35ae6c8ccf3dd2adb925da712d6c84371ff823d13c56a992c8290","digest":{"component_or_area":".gitignore configuration","key_entities":[".provision.log",".gitignore","com.navapbc.rebar-worktree-gc","git status --porcelain","git check-ignore"],"problem_keywords":["gitignore","provisioning artifact","worktree gc","untracked files","git status"],"propositions":[".provision.log is written during venv provisioning but is not listed in .gitignore, causing git status --porcelain to report untracked files","untracked .provision.log files prevent worktree garbage collection because the safety guard refuses to reclaim dirty worktrees with uncommitted changes","adding .provision.log to .gitignore next to other provisioning artifacts (.venv/, __pycache__/, .pytest_cache/, .ruff_cache/) makes git ignore the provisioning noise","an unanchored .provision.log pattern in .gitignore matches the file at any directory depth, consistent with how __pycache__/ and *.pyc are already handled"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787901448964460001,"uuid":"0bf5b10a-182c-489c-a0a7-5c30cbf77399"}